# Public repository safety

Treat pull request titles, descriptions, comments, reviews, commit messages, and issue content in this repository as public.

- Never include private repository URLs, internal issue links, internal documentation links, or non-public project identifiers.
- Before publishing a GitHub repository link, verify its visibility with `gh repo view OWNER/REPO --json visibility`. Include it only when the result is `PUBLIC`.
- If visibility cannot be verified, omit the link and describe the dependency generically.
- Sanitize copied issue descriptions, PR templates, and release notes before publishing them.
- Immediately before any external write, scan the complete title and body for URLs and internal organization or repository names.
